# The hashed terms document: its keccak256 is an ON-CHAIN COMMITMENT
# (Source Registry metadataHash). The bytes must be identical everywhere —
# repo blob, Windows working copy, Linux deploy — so line endings are pinned
# to LF and never rewritten by autocrlf.
# PINNED BY PATTERN, not per file (2026-08-03): v2 shipped UNPINNED because the
# rule named v1 explicitly. With core.autocrlf=true the next fresh checkout on
# Windows would have materialised it with CRLF — +122 bytes, a completely
# different keccak256 — and the founder could have signed, on-chain, a hash
# matching no document served at the canonical URL. Every version, forever.
artifacts/studio/public/referral-program-terms-*.txt text eol=lf
